mandarin-summary: Distinguish general negation from non-occurrence and form polar questions.

''Objectives:'' Distinguish general negation from non-occurrence and form polar questions.


! Negation and questions

* 你学中文吗？ — Nǐ xué Zhōngwén ma? — Do you study Chinese?
* 我不吃饭。 — Wǒ bù chī fàn. — I don't eat / won't eat.
* 我没吃饭。 — Wǒ méi chī fàn. — I haven't eaten / didn't eat.

''Key analysis:'' Compare the event-structure implications of 不 (bù) and 没 (méi), rather than treating them as present/past conjugations.

